IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc2-prelim`
IMPORT `ssc2-factors`
IMPORT `ssc2-bereavement`

-- Tests for ssc2-bereavement.l4 (ss 37, 38, 39, 39A, 39C). Every expected value is written by hand from the text.
-- Money figures are INVENTED test inputs: the rates come from ss 44 to 45B and are not in this part.
-- Tax years begin on 6 April: 5 April 2000 is in the tax year that began in 1999, 10 April 2000 in the one
-- that began in 2000, and 1 January 1990 in the one that began in 1989.

§ `Tests -- fixtures`

GIVEN pa IS A DATE
GIVETH A Person
`s 38 test person attaining pensionable age on` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1960
    `sex` IS Woman
    `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS pa

GIVEN kind IS A `s 39A Kind of survivor`
      member IS A BOOLEAN
      qualifies IS A BOOLEAN
      days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 39A Candidate`
`s 39A test candidate` MEANS `s 39A Candidate` WITH
    `s 39A(3B) the kind of survivor` IS kind
    `s 39A(3C) is a member of the same household as the deceased` IS member
    `s 39A(3D) is pregnant or entitled to child benefit as described in subsection (2)` IS qualifies
    `s 39A(3D)(c) the number of days as a member of the same household as the deceased` IS days

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Tax year`
`s 39 test tax year beginning in` MEANS `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS y

§ `Tests -- the Kleene helpers`

#ASSERT `s 37 both` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 37 both` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 37 both` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 37 both` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 37 either` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 37 either` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 37 either` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 37 either` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

