§ `Tests -- s 39(1), (2), (2A), (5), (6)`

#ASSERT `s 39(1) the additional pension falls to be calculated under section 45 by virtue of this section` `widowed mother's allowance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39(1) the additional pension falls to be calculated under section 45 by virtue of this section` `widow's pension` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39(1) the additional pension falls to be calculated under section 45 by virtue of this section` `widowed parent's allowance` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39(1) the additional pension falls to be calculated under section 45 by virtue of this section` `child benefit` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): the husband attained pensionable age on 1 January 1990
#ASSERT `s 39(2) the husband was over pensionable age when he died` (`s 38 test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 1990)) (Date 1 1 1990)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 39(2) the husband was over pensionable age when he died` (`s 38 test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 1990)) (Date 31 12 1989))
-- over pensionable age when he died: the tax year of attaining it (1 January 1990 is in the tax year that began in 1989)
#ASSERT (`s 39(2) the tax year read as the tax year in which the pensioner attained pensionable age` (`s 38 test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 1990)) (Date 15 1 2000))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 1989
-- under pensionable age when he died: the tax year of his death
#ASSERT (`s 39(2) the tax year read as the tax year in which the pensioner attained pensionable age` (`s 38 test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 2030)) (Date 15 1 2000))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 1999
#ASSERT (`s 39(2) the tax year read as the tax year in which the pensioner attained pensionable age` (`s 38 test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 2030)) (Date 10 4 2000))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT (`s 39(2) the tax year read as the tax year in which the pensioner attained pensionable age` (`s 38 test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 2030)) (Date 5 4 2000))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 1999
#ASSERT `s 39(2A) the amount read in place of the first amount specified in section 44(4) in pounds` (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 39(2A) the amount read in place of the first amount specified in section 44(4) in pounds` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): arguments: she qualified under s 38(1)(a), the day the husband died, the day she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance
#ASSERT `s 39(5) the time when the applicable qualifying condition was fulfilled` TRUE (Date 1 1 1990) (JUST (Date 5 5 1995)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 1990)
#ASSERT `s 39(5) the time when the applicable qualifying condition was fulfilled` FALSE (Date 1 1 1990) (JUST (Date 5 5 1995)) EQUALS JUST (Date 5 5 1995)
#ASSERT `s 39(5) the time when the applicable qualifying condition was fulfilled` FALSE (Date 1 1 1990) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39(6) the age read in subsection (4)` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 39(6) the age read in subsection (4)` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS 55
#ASSERT `s 39(6) the age read in subsection (4)` NOTHING EQUALS 55

§ `Tests -- s 39(4): the reduction for a widow under 55`

-- arguments: the rate apart from (4), the age read (55 or 50), her age in completed years at the time
-- 7 per cent of 100 for each year short of 55: 54 is 1 year short (93), 50 is 5 years short (65), 45 is 10 years short (30)
#ASSERT `s 39(4) the weekly rate of the widow's pension after any reduction in pounds` (JUST 100) 55 54 EQUALS JUST 93
#ASSERT `s 39(4) the weekly rate of the widow's pension after any reduction in pounds` (JUST 100) 55 50 EQUALS JUST 65
#ASSERT `s 39(4) the weekly rate of the widow's pension after any reduction in pounds` (JUST 100) 55 45 EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `s 39(4) the weekly rate of the widow's pension after any reduction in pounds` (JUST 120) 55 45 EQUALS JUST 36
-- 55 or over: not reduced
#ASSERT `s 39(4) the weekly rate of the widow's pension after any reduction in pounds` (JUST 100) 55 55 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 39(4) the weekly rate of the widow's pension after any reduction in pounds` (JUST 100) 55 60 EQUALS JUST 100
-- the 1988 rule reads 50 for 55: 49 is 1 year short, 50 is not short
#ASSERT `s 39(4) the weekly rate of the widow's pension after any reduction in pounds` (JUST 100) 50 49 EQUALS JUST 93
#ASSERT `s 39(4) the weekly rate of the widow's pension after any reduction in pounds` (JUST 100) 50 50 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 39(4) the weekly rate of the widow's pension after any reduction in pounds` (JUST 100) 50 41 EQUALS JUST 37
#ASSERT `s 39(4) the weekly rate of the widow's pension after any reduction in pounds` NOTHING 55 45 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 39A(1): when the section applies`

-- arguments: the day the spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner died, the day s 30 of the Pensions Act 2014 comes into force (6 April 2017, an input), married or partnered again before that day, the person
#ASSERT `s 39A(1) the section applies` (Date 1 3 2017) (Date 6 4 2017) FALSE (`s 38 test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 2030)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39A(1) the section applies` (Date 5 4 2017) (Date 6 4 2017) FALSE (`s 38 test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 2030)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39A(1) the section applies` (Date 6 4 2017) (Date 6 4 2017) FALSE (`s 38 test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 2030)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39A(1) the section applies` (Date 1 3 2017) (Date 6 4 2017) TRUE (`s 38 test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 1 1 2030)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39A(1) the section applies` (Date 1 3 2017) (Date 6 4 2017) FALSE (`s 38 test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 6 4 2017)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 39A(1) the section applies` (Date 1 3 2017) (Date 6 4 2017) FALSE (`s 38 test person attaining pensionable age on` (Date 7 4 2017)) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Tests -- s 39A(2), (3): the requirements`

-- arguments: son or daughter, the deceased was entitled to child benefit, residing together, the survivor was then entitled
#ASSERT `s 39A(3) the child or qualifying young person falls within this subsection` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39A(3) the child or qualifying young person falls within this subsection` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39A(3) the child or qualifying young person falls within this subsection` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 39A(3) the child or qualifying young person falls within this subsection` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- arguments: kind, the survivor is a woman, entitled to child benefit (a), pregnant by the deceased (b)(i), s 37(1)(c) circumstances (b)(ii), residing together (c)(i), artificially inseminated (c)(ii)
